diff --git a/docs/prefix-cache-offload.md b/docs/prefix-cache-offload.md
index 83a5ec7..9db8909 100644
--- a/docs/prefix-cache-offload.md
+++ b/docs/prefix-cache-offload.md
@@ -53,6 +53,18 @@ CPU-mapped destination and the page planes are mapped only on the GPU side.
 A GPUDirect Storage transport could remove payload staging; its indexes and
 I/O control structures would still occupy host memory.
 
+For a bounded correctness diagnostic, `flare run --verify-host-cache-transfers`
+or `[prefix_cache] verify_transfers = true` in Ignition checks every staged page
+plane and row copy against its source before the rank reports completion. The
+default is off. Enabled startup reports 32 MiB of scratch per rank, and each
+completed rank job logs direction, page/row presence, checked bytes and copies,
+and failures without logging payloads or addresses. A meaningful diagnostic
+run needs positive outbound and inbound checked bytes on every rank, with a
+row and pages present and zero failures. The added readbacks and waits change
+transfer timing, so performance measurements use the default-off setting.
+The diagnostic accepts a memory-only or disk-only store; a composite has two
+transfer sets and is rejected under the diagnostic's 32 MiB-per-rank bound.
+
 ## 2. Design
 
 ### 2.1 Checkpoint bytes
